  "description_blocks": [
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "Introduction"
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The Single-Axis Joystick Module is a 1-channel analog input module. It automatically returns to the center position. Compared to a Dual-Axis Joystick Module, the single-axis joystick moves in only one direction and outputs a single analog signal, making it ideal for use as a control lever in various scenarios that require speed control or position control with automatic centering — especially when the control logic of these motions needs to remain independent."
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "For example, in a vehicle model, one single-axis joystick module can be used to control the speed of movement, and another to control the steering; or in a tower crane model, a single-axis joystick module can control the lifting of the hook; or in a tracked vehicle model, two single-axis joystick modules can be used to independently control the speed of each track."
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "Important Notices"
    },
    {
      "kind": "bullet",
      "text": "Included accessory: The product comes with a 100mm Wire with 3Pin SH1.0 Connectors."
    },
    {
      "kind": "bullet",
      "text": "Choking hazard: This product contains small parts. Keep out of reach of children to avoid accidental ingestion."
    }
  ],
